cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "From Machine Learning to Foundation Models: Hands-On Artificial Intelligence for Power & Energy Systems"
message: "If you use this course in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Steffen
    family-names: Kortmann
    email: steffen.kortmann@fit.fraunhofer.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A ten-notebook university course tracing the development of modern artificial
  intelligence from classical supervised learning to foundation models, using
  electric power and energy systems as the recurring application domain. Each
  method is implemented from scratch before the production library is
  introduced. The course argues that foundation models are a broader paradigm
  than large language models, and closes by pretraining a small graph-based
  foundation model across several electrical networks and transferring it to an
  unseen grid topology.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - deep learning
  - foundation models
  - transformers
  - graph neural networks
  - power systems
  - energy forecasting
  - teaching materials
  - reproducible research
